From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: win32u: the interface fonts' names are families, as Windows keeps them

SystemParametersInfo(SPI_GETNONCLIENTMETRICS) and the icon title font gave
the enumerated face's full name ("Inter Regular", also for a bold caption
font) in place of the family's. Programs look the name up as a family:
Firefox found none for CSS system-ui and drew its pages in a serif font.

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -4886,8 +4886,12 @@
                     &count, &enum_entry );
     release_display_dc( hdc );
 
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the family's name, as Windows keeps it ("Segoe UI"),
+     * not the face's full name ("Inter Regular", "Tahoma Bold"): programs
+     * look the name up as a family. Firefox found no family "Inter Regular"
+     * for its system-ui font and fell back to a serif one */
     if (count)
-        lstrcpyW( fullname, enum_entry.lf.elfFullName );
+        lstrcpyW( fullname, enum_entry.lf.elfLogFont.lfFaceName );
     else
         lstrcpyW( fullname, lf->lfFaceName );
 }
